+# 2026-11-24-writing-spending-sources
+
+English | [中文](2026-11-24-writing-spending-sources.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Adds the mode-dossiers and spend-limit source kinds to persisted messages.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-11-24-writing-spending-sources
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:agent/inbox/spliced"
+    previous: "2026-11-19-cua-input-notices"
+    after: "7d45665297b57c40dc768a25e81be661579e363db61e2f6dd69ddeef480d9a3f"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:developer/message"
+    previous: "2026-11-19-cua-input-notices"
+    after: "51fec3954ebea109d5d45a4131cbb1700a8d1ce749005032df34993922c37a1b"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:session/title-llm-request"
+    previous: "2026-11-19-cua-input-notices"
+    after: "d6764b2c9bd802634762f2d0c50d865ae56ae9fd00c8aec26a47d9776e8dd7cd"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:user/message"
+    previous: "2026-11-19-cua-input-notices"
+    after: "5b789bab5bdbdfd5609fbaa7fe7712fc8871f7d9fe0509675e21baf4bf2438fb"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+Existing v4 messages retain all fields. Writing selections and continuation notices use ordinary user/message events with text content. The upstream Session reader selects by event type, preserves the source, and reads both messages without these plugins. Older clients can display their text. Rebuilding the writing projection and deduplicating a resumed pause require the corresponding plugin. A missing pauseId is valid and cannot match a later identified pause. The SQLite spending ledger has its own schema version.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+The writing.spec.ts v4 round trip reads an ordinary prompt alone and in a log with both new source kinds using the unchanged upstream Session reader. All eight writing tests passed. The Web writing-spending.e2e.ts test compared stored messages with the dispatched request and observed one continuation after reopening a blocked conversation.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
