+---
+description: "Workspace writing materials, version-checked editing and logged request context for the Writing preset."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# Writing materials
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+The owner manages Markdown files in a registered workspace. The Writing preset reads selected voice cards from `story/style/` and story references from `story/bible/`. The registry at `story/materials.json` stores titles and selection. The Standard preset receives no writing material from this package.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Editing and selection](#editing-and-selection)
+- [Model experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known limitations and deferred work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+
+<a id="editing-and-selection"></a>
+
+## Editing and selection
+
+The `modeDossiers` Remote offers `inventory`, `createStory`, `adoptStory`, `readStory`, `writeStory`, `selectStory` and `removeStory`. Each operation names a registered workspace. Creation selects the new document. Existing files can be adopted into the registry. Removing an entry keeps its Markdown file. A write must carry the version returned by the read and reports a conflict after a competing edit.
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+
+## Model Experience
+
+### Selected workspace documents
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+Each changed selection is logged as a user message with the `mode-dossiers` source. The next Writing step reissues selected documents if compaction removed them, and clearing a previously admitted selection records a withdrawal. Reopening the conversation reconstructs admission from its log. The inclusive UTF-8 limit is 16 KiB by default and a value of zero disables admission.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Selected Markdown consumes input tokens up to the configured UTF-8 byte limit.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Existing message prefixes remain reusable. A changed selection or compaction appends new text at the end of the conversation.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- A missing or corrupt material store may omit the optional context from that step. The Host logs the read failure. Open **Settings → Writing materials** to manage the workspace library.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Maintenance notes</summary>
+
+None.
+
+</details>
