+---
+description: "The Writing materials settings page manages a workspace’s voice cards and story references."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# Writing materials settings
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Choose a workspace under **Settings → Writing materials**. Create a voice card or story reference, edit its Markdown, and select the documents for Writing mode. Removing a document from the library keeps the Markdown file.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Workspace library](#workspace-library)
+
+<a id="workspace-library"></a>
+## Workspace library
+
+Changing the workspace loads its own library. Saving after another editor has changed the document reports a conflict. The Host owns selection, version checks and admission into the conversation. [Writing materials](../../api/mode-dossiers/README.md)
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+### Workspace selection
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+Checking a `story/` file makes it eligible for the next Writing request. Viewing Settings sends no request to the model.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Selected documents contribute input tokens when the Host admits them.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Navigating the settings page leaves the request prefix unchanged.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- Only the application owner can manage the registered workspace library from this page.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Maintenance notes</summary>
+
+None.
+
+</details>
