+---
+description: "Shared rolling CNY budgets for model requests and native search on one host."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# Spending limits
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Enable rolling budgets in Settings. A request may proceed when all enabled windows can cover its reservation.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Charging and recovery](#charging-and-recovery)
+
+<a id="charging-and-recovery"></a>
+## Charging and recovery
+
+The local SQLite ledger serializes reservations across processes. Set the ledger path, polling interval, per-provider rates, context size and search cost in the plugin configuration. The ledger estimates input and output cost before dispatch and settles against reported usage. An incomplete response retains the reserved cost. A recovered process reservation starts its rolling period at recovery. Unknown rates or ledger failures block chargeable requests when limits apply.
+
+### Recovery and upgrades
+
+Each window has an independent amount, enabled state and reset point. Resetting a window retains in-flight reservations and leaves other windows active. Disabling a limit retains its history. Automatic continuation restores eligible Standard and Writing conversations through their lifecycle owner. An identified, durably recorded notice prevents duplicate delivery. An archived conversation stays paused.
+
+Ledger schema v3 migrates v1 and v2 balances, reservations and preferences. Close other writers before upgrading. Older processes cannot write v3 ledgers.
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+### Budget recovery notice
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+A resumed conversation receives a logged user message with the `spend-limit` source and the pause identity.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Only the continuation text contributes additional input tokens.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+The notice appends to the existing conversation prefix.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- The ledger estimates spending on this host. Provider invoices, external requests and requests dispatched while all limits are disabled are outside its totals. A reservation can exceed the final cost.
+- Pending settlements, manual pauses and a request larger than a configured limit can prevent a reliable estimate of the next resume time. The ledger requires a local filesystem.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Maintenance notes</summary>
+
+None.
+
+</details>
